{title: Abide with Me}
{artist: Henry Francis Lyte / William Henry Monk}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Meditative, Closing}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 481장}
{title_ko: 때 저물어서 날이 어두니}
{score: abide-with-me.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Abide with me; fast [C]falls the [G]eventide
The [G]darkness deepens; [D]Lord, with me a[G]bide
When [G]other helpers [C]fail and [G]comforts flee
Help of the [C]helpless, [D]O a[G]bide with me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Swift to its close ebbs [C]out life's [G]little day
Earth's [G]joys grow dim, its [D]glories pass a[G]way
[G]Change and decay in [C]all a[G]round I see
O Thou who [C]changest not, [D]a[G]bide with me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I need Thy presence [C]every [G]passing hour
What [G]but Thy grace can [D]foil the tempter's [G]power
[G]Who like Thyself my [C]guide and [G]stay can be
Through cloud and [C]sunshine, [D]O a[G]bide with me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]I fear no foe, with [C]Thee at [G]hand to bless
Ills [G]have no weight, and [D]tears no bitter[G]ness
[G]Where is death's sting? [C]Where, grave, thy [G]victory
I tri[C]umph still, if [D]Thou a[G]bide with me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Hold Thou Thy cross be[C]fore my [G]closing eyes
Shine [G]through the gloom and [D]point me to the [G]skies
[G]Heaven's morning breaks, and [C]earth's vain [G]shadows flee
In life, in [C]death, O [D]Lord, a[G]bide with me
{end_of_verse}
